      "writtenOn": "2024-02-16T14:19:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Q: should we guard with `cfg!(llpvm_changes)` instead?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "a46005a680422dfd3218ecd603926c4b9b244523",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "836deb31_fd876550",
        "filename": "vm/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-16T14:38:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This tool is called from many host tests. In order to correctly flag this, I\u0027m allowing this `instance_id` to be an Option.\n\nThe accessor `instance_id(\u0026self)` will throw error is cfg!(llpvm_changes) is set \u0026 instance_id is not input.",
      "parentUuid": "5d6b74f6_770699cc",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "a46005a680422dfd3218ecd603926c4b9b244523",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d19b3f93_6deecff8",
        "filename": "vm/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1432579
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-16T15:51:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We usually hide the argument from the cli until the feature is enabled. This reduces confusion for developers, who see the arg, try to use it, and get an error \"not implemented\" as a response.\n\nPlease follow the approach of other flag-guarded arguments (e.g. extra_apks) and use `[cfg(llpvm_changes)]`",
      "parentUuid": "836deb31_fd876550",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "a46005a680422dfd3218ecd603926c4b9b244523",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c743025_3600c7cd",
        "filename": "vm/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-16T16:15:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e We usually hide the argument from the cli until the feature is enabled\n\nThat makes sense, but for the purpose of automated testing, how would the host know if the feature is enabled \u0026 accordingly set flag (ex MicrodroidHostTests)?",
      "parentUuid": "d19b3f93_6deecff8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "a46005a680422dfd3218ecd603926c4b9b244523",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92d2615c_c2ce7b36",
        "filename": "vm/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-16T17:09:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "How about we add \"vm --check-feature-enabled \u003cfoo\u003e\", which calls IVirtualizationService#isFeatureEnabled ? \nIt can return non-zero if not.\n\n(This is easier in MicrodroidTests)",
      "parentUuid": "0c743025_3600c7cd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "a46005a680422dfd3218ecd603926c4b9b244523",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "41824c56_1a5ace7a",
        "filename": "vm/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1897307
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-16T17:40:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e How about we add \"vm --check-feature-enabled \u003cfoo\u003e\"\n\nSo, the host will need to interpret the result of this command \u0026 accordingly set flag in vm `run-app`?\n\nAnd how will Host know what string to compose with `check-feature-enabled`? And I guess the VM binary can contain a list of all enabled feature strings.\n\nAnd I think, `check-feature-enabled` must not be feature flagged because it will be executed irrespective of other flags (such as llpvm) being enabled.\n\n\nI do like this idea, it is generalized, however we are introducing additional unflagged `check-feature-enabled` command to support this \u0026 I would like to avoid it unless we need other feature flag knowledge in Host. Wdyt?",
      "parentUuid": "92d2615c_c2ce7b36",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "a46005a680422dfd3218ecd603926c4b9b244523",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0742e48f_fc6f599a",
        "filename": "vm/src/main.rs",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 170,
      "author": {
        "id": 1060831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-16T17:59:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e So, the host will need to interpret the result of this command \u0026 accordingly set flag in vm run-app?\n\nYes. The command can just succeed or fail, or we can interpret its output.\n\n\u003e And how will Host know what string to compose with check-feature-enabled?\n\nWell, we know what we\u0027ve called all the features.\n\n\u003e And I think, check-feature-enabled must not be feature flagged because it will be executed irrespective of other flags (such as llpvm) being enabled.\n\nYes.\n\n\u003e I do like this idea, it is generalized, however we are introducing additional unflagged check-feature-enabled command to support this\n\nGiven the vm command is only used for tests the risk seems low.\n\n\u003e I would like to avoid it unless we need other feature flag knowledge in Host\n\nWe need it here.\n\nAnd I\u0027m slightly surprised we haven\u0027t needed it before.",
      "parentUuid": "41824c56_1a5ace7a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 170,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 170,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "a46005a680422dfd3218ecd603926c4b9b244523",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
